<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">CAPABILITIES, WITHOUT THE HYPE</p><h1>A framework you can understand.</h1><p>These are the components present in this repository today. Maturity varies; read the status before adopting a feature.</p><div class="status-legend"><span class="status status-implemented">Implemented</span><span class="status status-experimental">Experimental</span><span class="status status-planned">Planned</span></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container feature-list">
    <article><span class="status status-implemented">Implemented</span><h2>HTTP application lifecycle</h2><p>Bootstrap configuration and routes, create requests and responses, dispatch through middleware, and handle exceptions centrally.</p><a href="/docs">Read the framework guide →</a></article>
    <article><span class="status status-implemented">Implemented</span><h2>Routing and middleware</h2><p>Method-and-path routes, route parameters, 404 fallback handlers, method mismatch responses, and an ordered middleware pipeline.</p><a href="/architecture">View request flow →</a></article>
    <article><span class="status status-implemented">Implemented</span><h2>Configuration and environment</h2><p>PHP configuration files, environment loading, typed configuration validation, and environment-specific overrides.</p><a href="/docs/getting-started">Configure an application →</a></article>
    <article><span class="status status-implemented">Implemented</span><h2>Validation and safe templates</h2><p>Reusable input validation and an intentionally small template renderer with escaped variable interpolation and static includes.</p><a href="/docs">Explore the APIs →</a></article>
    <article><span class="status status-implemented">Implemented</span><h2>PDO database building blocks</h2><p>Parameterized query helpers, transaction support, migration execution, and migration status tooling. A live MySQL integration is not verified in this environment.</p><a href="/docs">See implementation status →</a></article>
    <article><span class="status status-experimental">Experimental</span><h2>Server-rendered reactive UI</h2><p>A framework-owned browser runtime sends registered actions to a PHP component and reconciles returned HTML. The current model is one session-owned page component, not a stable public API.</p><a href="/playground">Try the prototype →</a></article>
    <article><span class="status status-planned">Planned</span><h2>Authentication and authorization integration</h2><p>Session and CSRF building blocks exist. A complete framework-owned authentication and authorization system is not yet implemented.</p></article>
    <article><span class="status status-planned">Planned</span><h2>Reactive forms and navigation</h2><p>Field-level reactive validation, form submission, client-side navigation, shared state, and nested components are not part of the current prototype.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section section-muted"><div class="container small-callout"><div><h2>Want the implementation details?</h2><p>See feature maturity, verification status, and known limitations before you depend on an API.</p></div><a class="button button-primary" href="/docs">Read the docs <span>→</span></a></div></section>
